---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import places from '../../data/backlink-directory.json';
const categories = [...new Set(places.map(p => p.category))].sort();
---
<BaseLayout title="19 places to submit your product for SEO & AI discovery | Andrew Allsop" description="A free directory of product submission opportunities: APIs, MCP servers, extensions and integrations. Compare requirements and find official submission guidance.">
<section class="directory">
  <header><p class="eyebrow">FREE RESOURCE / PRODUCT DISTRIBUTION</p><h1>19 places to get your product discovered.</h1><p class="intro">A practical directory of backlink and distribution opportunities for SEO and AI discovery. Find the platforms that fit what you’ve already built.</p><p class="meta">Reviewed 2 November 2026 · 19 opportunities · No signup</p></header>
  <aside><strong>Start with product fit.</strong> Most of these platforms need a working integration, API, extension or plugin—not just a website URL. Build something useful for their users, then make your product easy to find.</aside>
  <div class="controls"><label>Search the directory<input id="search" type="search" placeholder="Try MCP, API, extension…" /></label><label>Category<select id="category"><option value="">All categories</option>{categories.map(c=><option>{c}</option>)}</select></label></div>
  <p id="count" role="status" aria-live="polite">19 opportunities</p>
  <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Product submission directory, scroll horizontally for all columns">
  <table><caption>Where to submit, what you need, and what to check</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Platform</th><th scope="col">What you need</th><th scope="col">How to get listed</th><th scope="col">Before you start</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  {places.map((p,i)=><tr data-entry data-category={p.category} data-search={`${p.name} ${p.category} ${p.requires} ${p.action}`.toLowerCase()}><th scope="row"><span class="number">{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><a href={p.url}>{p.name} ↗</a><small>{p.category}</small></th><td>{p.requires}</td><td>{p.action}<a class="guide" href={p.url}>Official site / guidance ↗</a></td><td>{p.note}<a class="source" href={p.source}>Original post ↗</a></td></tr>)}
  </tbody></table></div><p id="empty" hidden>No matches. Try a different search or category.</p>
  <section class="notes"><h2>Make the listing worth having.</h2><ol><li>Choose platforms your customers actually use.</li><li>Use a consistent product name, clear description and relevant website link.</li><li>Test the integration and provide documentation, privacy information and support.</li><li>Inspect your live listing: does it link to the right page, and is that page publicly accessible?</li><li>Track referral visits, activated users and conversions—not just the number of listings.</li></ol>
  <h2>Backlinks, SEO and AEO</h2><p>These are potential places to earn a product mention or link, not guaranteed ranking improvements. Link attributes and indexability vary by listing. The thread’s domain-rating scores and “dofollow” claims have not been independently audited and are not used to rank this directory.</p><p>For Google’s AI Overviews and AI Mode, the usual SEO fundamentals still apply: helpful content, crawlability and index eligibility. There is no extra technical requirement that makes a listing automatically eligible for an AI citation. <a href="https://developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/ai-features">Read Google’s guidance ↗</a></p>
  <h2>Sources and review notes</h2><p>Adapted from <a href="https://x.com/tarasshyn/status/2116573909839430019">Taras Shynkarenko’s series</a>. All 19 posts in the quoted chain were reviewed, from Zapier through EmDash, along with the available replies to the linked post. Each row links to the original post and platform guidance. Platform pages were checked where publicly accessible; account-gated and unverified details are flagged above. This is a source review, not a test submission to each platform.</p><p>The series also mentions <a href="https://libraries.io">Libraries.io</a>, <a href="https://npm.io">npm.io</a>, <a href="https://www.jsdelivr.com">jsDelivr</a> and <a href="https://deps.dev">deps.dev</a> as package discovery surfaces. Treat these as potential downstream coverage, not four guaranteed submissions. It also links to <a href="https://github.com/punkpeye/awesome-mcp-servers">Awesome MCP Servers</a>; check its contribution rules before suggesting your repository.</p></section>
</section>
</BaseLayout>
<script>
const search=document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#search')!;
const category=document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#category')!;
const rows=[...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLTableRowElement>('[data-entry]')];
function filter(){let count=0;for(const row of rows){const visible=(!category.value||row.dataset.category===category.value)&&(row.dataset.search||'').includes(search.value.trim().toLowerCase());row.hidden=!visible;if(visible)count++;}document.querySelector('#count')!.textContent=`${count} ${count===1?'opportunity':'opportunities'}`;(document.querySelector('#empty') as HTMLElement).hidden=count>0;}
search.addEventListener('input',filter);category.addEventListener('change',filter);
</script>
<style>
/* Keep this wider resource's entire shell aligned with its table. */
:global(body:has(.directory)){--directory-width:1100px;--directory-half:550px}
:global(body:has(.directory) .reading-rail),
:global(body:has(.directory) .cobalt-header-rail),
:global(body:has(.directory) .cobalt-header-ticker),
:global(body:has(.directory) .cobalt-header-nav),
:global(body:has(.directory) .global-cobalt-footer){width:100%;max-width:var(--directory-width);min-width:0}
:global(.reading-rail:has(.directory)){z-index:1}
:global(body:has(.directory) .dither-gutter-left){right:calc(50% + var(--directory-half))}
:global(body:has(.directory) .dither-gutter-right){left:calc(50% + var(--directory-half))}
:global(body:has(.directory) .cobalt-noise){mask-image:linear-gradient(to right,#000 calc(50% - 550px),transparent calc(50% - 550px),transparent calc(50% + 550px),#000 calc(50% + 550px));-webkit-mask-image:linear-gradient(to right,#000 calc(50% - 550px),transparent calc(50% - 550px),transparent calc(50% + 550px),#000 calc(50% + 550px))}
.directory{background:var(--cream);color:#202020;padding:clamp(20px,4vw,48px);position:relative}.directory header{padding:16px 0 32px}.eyebrow,.meta,.number,small,#count{font-family:monospace}.eyebrow{font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.12em;color:#1839af}h1{font-size:clamp(36px,5vw,62px);line-height:1.05;letter-spacing:-.045em;margin:20px 0}.intro{font-size:19px;line-height:1.6}.meta{font-size:12px;margin-top:22px;color:#555}aside{border-left:3px solid #1739b0;padding:18px;background:var(--cream-sunken);font-size:14px;line-height:1.7}.controls{display:flex;gap:16px;margin-top:30px;flex-wrap:wrap}label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;font-size:12px;font-weight:600;flex:1;min-width:180px}input,select{border:1px solid #aaa;background:var(--cream-raised);padding:12px;color:#202020;border-radius:0;font:inherit;font-size:15px;width:100%}#count{font-size:12px;margin:18px 0}.table-wrap{overflow-x:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;min-width:850px;text-align:left;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6}caption{text-align:left;padding:0 0 16px;font-weight:600}thead{background:#1939ad;color:white}th,td{padding:18px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--hairline);vertical-align:top}thead th{font-size:11px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em}tbody th{min-width:150px;width:19%}td{width:27%}td:nth-child(2){width:18%}tr[hidden]{display:none}tbody tr:nth-child(even){background:var(--cream-sunken)}a{text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px;color:#1739ad}thead a{color:white}.number{display:block;color:#777;font-size:10px;margin-bottom:6px}small{display:block;font-size:10px;font-weight:400;margin-top:9px}.guide,.source{display:block;font-size:11px;margin-top:12px}.notes{margin-top:48px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.8}h2{font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;margin:32px 0 16px;letter-spacing:-.025em}.notes p{margin:14px 0}ol{padding-left:20px;list-style:decimal}li{margin:8px 0}:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #1739ad;outline-offset:3px}
</style>
